From 90410caa3f13b8ed05644bb74df8af92153c8a4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:36:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] MIG-12 phase 4: seal self-check clean; ledger unfold site
 re-pointed; warnings pruned

All 20 ledger definitions elaborate with [local irreducible] and zero errors
(seal-all6), certifying every per-definition definitional-site count at 0. The
round cell-word endpoint is read through a configuration-generalized cellWord,
so the gs endpoint is an instantiation at a.apply c rather than a default-simp
pass over an Action.apply application. The ledger's one explicit unfold row
(fieldOffset, exists_recordEqTM) and the offsets_aux induction both re-point to
the new recordStep_fieldOffset_congr, assembled from fieldOffset_zero and
fieldOffset_cons_succ. Warning prune: 12 seam sites drop unused
recordStep_mapState_mk/Option.map_some, one unused simp arg and one unused
binder renamed. Real check: 0 errors, 0 warnings (check-groupI).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012MLwzCawbbQRBmmECNRLGQ
